677 0 obj
<<
/A 2400 0 R
/Alt (The two panel diagram shows European regions with mortality data and climate season with LST data from 2000 to 2023. Panel a displays a map of Europe with major regions and cities. A color scale indicates mortality in deaths per million, ranging from less than 100 \(light blue\) to greater than 250 \(dark red\). An inset map shows Europe within a global context. A horizontal scale bar indicates kilometers from 0 to 1200. Panel b shows a vertical bar graph of climate season in Europe. Months from January to November are listed on the vertical axis. A red bar highlights the warm season from May to September, corresponding to weeks 18 to 40. To the right, two stacks of maps represent 504 daytime and 504 nighttime images of Europe, illustrating 2000 to 2023 LST data from MODIS. Below these, two maps of Europe show pixel level maximum LST. The top map shows daytime LST ranging from 12.7 degrees Celsius to 58.3 degrees Celsius. The bottom map shows nighttime LST ranging from 2.3 degrees Celsius to 34.5 degrees Celsius.)
/K 6
/P 44 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
