740 0 obj
<<
/A 2449 0 R
/Alt (This flowchart details cumulative heat effects impact modeling across five steps: Data Acquisition, Preprocessing, Feature Extraction, Statistical Modeling, and Result and Analysis. Data acquisition uses MOD11A1 LST, ERA5-Land Temperature, and Eurostat mortality records. Preprocessing handles missing data via linear interpolation, validates imputation, and merges data into a CSV. Feature extraction calculates D_LST, N_LST, TDif, Tmean, and Cumulative Index PAT. Statistical modeling adjusts PAT from 100 percent to 0, determines optimal PAT, adjusts weekly data, and determines cumulative days using a random forest model with 5-fold cross validation. Results show spatial distribution at the same temperature range, accumulated temperature enhances model performance, and cumulative heat effects on mortality persist for 4 weeks. No significant difference exists between satellite and reanalysis data. A scatter plot of predicted versus true mortality shows R squared equals 0.623 and RMSE equals 32.147 deaths per million. Key findings: nighttime heat exposure and accumulated heat exposure are important for health risks, previous weeks temperature contributes 70 percent, and the model performs well on 90 independent validation sites.)
/K 5
/P 44 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
