/A 2456 0 R
/Alt (Four-panel graph shows relative risk of death vs. temperature. Panel a: Daytime relative risk for both sexes, men, and women. Risk is highest at low temps, lowest around 30C, then increases. D_LST frequency peaks around 30C. Deaths increase from 15-40C, then decrease. Panel b: Nighttime relative risk for both sexes, men, and women. Risk is highest at low temps, lowest around 20C, then increases. N_LST frequency peaks around 20C. Deaths increase from 5-25C, then decrease. Panel c: Daytime relative risk for age groups 0-14, 15-59, 60-79, and 80&#x0002B;. Risk is highest at low temps, lowest around 30C, then increases. 80&#x0002B; group shows highest risk at both extremes. Deaths increase from 15-40C, then decrease. Panel d: Nighttime relative risk for age groups 0-14, 15-59, 60-79, and 80&#x0002B;. Risk is highest at low temps, lowest around 20C, then increases. 80&#x0002B; group shows highest risk at both extremes. Deaths increase from 5-25C, then decrease.)
