/A 2470 0 R
/Alt (The 3-panel figure shows model performance. Panel a is a scatter plot with a fitted curve, showing R squared on the vertical axis from 0.62 to 0.69 and Proportion of accumulate temperature, PAT, on the horizontal axis from 0 percent to 100 percent. The curve rises from 0.63 at 0 percent PAT, peaks at 0.679 at 70 percent PAT, then declines to 0.66 at 100 percent PAT. Points are colored by rRMSE, ranging from 11 percent to 15 percent. Panel b is a horizontal bar graph showing Importance rate on the horizontal axis from 0 percent to 20 percent and Feature on the vertical axis. N LST has the highest importance rate at approximately 20 percent, followed by D LST at approximately 18 percent. Other features like N LST AT1, D LST AT1, LST Mean, LST Dif, N LST AT2, D LST AT2, N LST AT3, and D LST AT3 show decreasing importance rates. Panel c is a heatmap with cities on the horizontal axis and Input combination on the vertical axis, including Night3, Night2, Night1, Night0, Day3, Day2, Day1, Day0, Com3, Com2, Com1, Com0, and Average. The heatmap shows varying values from 0.2 to 0.8, with brighter regions indicating higher values.)
