/Alt (The three panel figure shows R squared and rRMSE of mortality estimates across Europe and performance metrics for different inputs. Panel a displays a map of Europe with R squared values for mortality estimates. A legend indicates R squared values from 0.10 to 0.20, 0.20 to 0.30, 0.30 to 0.40, 0.40 to 0.50, 0.50 to 0.60, and greater than 0.60. Insets show magnified views of England, Poland, and Belgium and the Netherlands. Panel b displays a map of Europe with rRMSE percentage values for mortality estimates. A legend indicates rRMSE values from 0.0 to 7.0, 7.0 to 9.0, 9.0 to 11, 11 to 13, 13 to 15, and greater than 15. Insets show magnified views of England, Poland, and Belgium and the Netherlands. Panel c contains two grouped scatter plots. The top plot shows R squared values on the vertical axis from 0.0 to 0.6. The horizontal axis shows three groups: dayLST, nightLST, and dayLST plus nightLST. Each group has subcategories of Total, Man, and Woman. The R squared values generally range from 0.3 to 0.5 across all categories. The bottom plot shows rRMSE percentage values on the vertical axis from 0 to 30. The horizontal axis has the same three groups and subcategories. The rRMSE values generally range from 10 to 20 percent across all categories.)
