/A 2519 0 R
/Alt (The four panel figure, arranged two by two, shows R squared spatial distribution for mortality rates and a scatter plot. Panel a, titled Estimation of total mortality rate, displays a map of Europe with regions shaded based on R squared values, ranging from less than 0.40 to greater than 0.80. Inset maps show England and Belgium and Netherlands. Panel b, titled Estimation of men mortality rate, shows a similar map with R squared values for men. Panel c, titled Estimation of women mortality rate, presents another map with R squared values for women. Panel d, titled Performance of estimated mortality rate, is a scatter plot with True mortality on the horizontal axis and Predicted mortality on the vertical axis, both ranging from 0 to 800. The plot shows a dense cluster of points along a diagonal line, indicating a strong correlation. A solid diagonal line represents the ideal prediction, and a dashed line shows the actual trend. The R squared value is 0.584 and RMSE is 35.276 death per million.)
/K 1
/P 44 0 R
/Pg 27 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
